.TH HEALTHCHECK\-HTTP 1 "2026-09" "init-toolkit" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
healthcheck-http \- HEALTHCHECK-friendly HTTP probe
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B healthcheck-http
.I URL
.RI [ timeout-seconds ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Probes one URL and exits 0 when it answers healthily, for use as a
container
.B HEALTHCHECK
without pulling curl and a shell pipeline into the image.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The endpoint answered.
.TP
.B 1
It did not, or the timeout expired.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
As a Docker HEALTHCHECK:
.PP
.RS
.B HEALTHCHECK CMD healthcheck-http http://localhost:8080/healthz 3
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wait-for (1),
.BR healthcheck-tcp (1).
Project documentation:
https://github.com/fabiocicerchia/init-toolkit
